kh-ramabs: a point32le layout, for guests that keep the pointer as two int32

BeOS R5's app_server keeps its pointer coordinate as two little-endian
int32 fields, where Rhapsody DR2 keeps a Point{int16 x, int16 y}.  The
device's read and write accessors are the only two places that know a wire
format, so a second layout is one branch in each plus the realize-time
string parse; nothing else in kh-ramabs changes and no VMStateDescription
is added, so `-device kh-ramabs` still leaves a station's device set and
its golden checkpoint untouched.

Derived and proven on beos: see docs/lab/BEOS-ABSOLUTE-POINTER.md.

Signed-off-by: osgallery contributors <noreply@example.com>

Index: b/hw/misc/kh-ramabs.c
